       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">NATIONAL</span> · News18 India · 2026-09-20 · editor 9/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>Chilling WhatsApp Message Emerges in Yuvraj Manchanda Murder Probe</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#Yuvraj Manchanda</span> <span>#Murder Probe</span> <span>#Fraud Case</span> <span>#WhatsApp Message</span></div>
       <p>A disturbing WhatsApp message, containing the phrase “Sell your wife, do anything,” has reportedly surfaced as a critical piece of evidence in the ongoing investigation into the murder of Yuvraj Manchanda. The revelation links directly to an alleged Rs 1.2 crore fraud case, with the accused in Manchanda's murder also implicated in the financial scam.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-09-20/chilling-whatsapp-message-emerges-in-yuvraj-manchanda-murder.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>Police sources indicate that the chilling message is now a central focus of their probe, aiming to uncover its origin, context, and relevance to both the homicide and the extensive financial irregularities. The emergence of such a message suggests a potentially desperate or coercive dynamic at play within the alleged fraud scheme, adding a grim dimension to the investigation.</p><p>Investigators are meticulously examining digital footprints and communications to establish connections between the various parties involved in the fraud and their potential roles in Manchanda’s death. The financial motive appears to be a significant line of inquiry, with the WhatsApp message potentially shedding light on the extreme pressures or demands associated with the alleged scam.</p><p>The case has drawn considerable public attention due to its complex nature, intertwining murder, fraud, and now, highly unusual digital communication. Law enforcement officials have confirmed that the investigation is active and comprehensive, with all leads being pursued to bring clarity to the circumstances surrounding Manchanda's demise and the associated financial crimes.</p><p>What to watch: The police investigation will focus on the message's origin and its connection to the fraud and murder cases.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: Article stays consistent with source summary, adding reasonable context.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
