     <article class="story single" data-beat="national">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">NATIONAL</span> · The Hindu · 2026-09-20 · editor 9/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>Govt jobs to one lakh youth in Uttar Pradesh, says Adityanath</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#Uttar Pradesh</span> <span>#Yogi Adityanath</span> <span>#Government Jobs</span> <span>#UPSSSC</span></div>
       <p>Uttar Pradesh Chief Minister Yogi Adityanath has announced plans to create approximately one lakh government jobs for the state’s youth. The announcement aims to address long-standing concerns regarding employment opportunities and career stability for graduates seeking public sector positions.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-09-20/govt-jobs-to-one-lakh-youth-in-uttar-pradesh-says-adityanath.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>The recruitment drive will be executed through two primary channels. The Uttar Pradesh Subordinate Services Selection Commission (UPSSSC) is expected to announce results for 25,000 to 30,000 positions. Additionally, the Uttar Pradesh Education Selection Commission (UPESC) will handle recruitments for another 20,000 to 25,000 roles, specifically within the education sector.</p><p>This move is part of a broader strategy to enhance the state’s public sector infrastructure and provide secure livelihoods to its large youth population. The government has emphasized that these positions will be filled based on merit and transparent selection processes, ensuring fairness for all applicants.</p><p>The announcement has been received positively by student groups and political stakeholders who have long advocated for increased public sector employment. Officials have assured that the recruitment processes will be monitored closely to prevent any irregularities and to ensure timely appointments.</p><p>The initiative reflects the state government’s commitment to economic development and social welfare, aiming to reduce out-migration of skilled youth from the state.</p><p>What to watch: The specific dates for the issuance of merit lists and the commencement of the joining process for the selected candidates.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The article correctly synthesizes the recruitment numbers from the source and attributes the announcement to Adityanath as implied by the headline, with no contradictory or invented claims.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://www.thehindu.com/news/national/uttar-pradesh/govt-jobs-to-one-lakh-youth-in-uttar-pradesh-says-adityanath/article71487054.ece" rel="noopener">The Hindu</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
