     <article class="story single" data-beat="national">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">NATIONAL</span> · India Today · 2026-09-20 · editor 9/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>Tragedy Strikes Mumbai Ganpati Pandal: 2 Dead, 6 Injured in Electrocution</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#Mumbai</span> <span>#Ganpati Pandal</span> <span>#Electrocution</span> <span>#Kala Chowki</span></div>
       <p>A tragic incident at a Ganpati pandal in Mumbai's Kala Chowki area has resulted in the deaths of two individuals and left six others injured due to electrocution. The unfortunate event occurred at a site prepared for the upcoming Ganpati festival, casting a somber mood over the preparations.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-09-20/tragedy-strikes-mumbai-ganpati-pandal-2-dead-6-injured-in-el.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>Emergency services were immediately dispatched to the scene following reports of the incident. The injured were swiftly transported to nearby medical facilities for treatment, with their conditions currently being monitored. Authorities have initiated a thorough investigation to ascertain the precise cause of the electrical malfunction that led to the fatalities and injuries.</p><p>Preliminary inquiries are expected to focus on the electrical wiring, temporary installations, and overall safety protocols implemented at the pandal. Such incidents during festive setups raise serious questions about adherence to safety standards and the oversight mechanisms in place to prevent preventable accidents. The local administration and event organizers are likely to face scrutiny regarding the measures taken to ensure public safety.</p><p>The tragedy serves as a stark reminder of the critical importance of rigorous safety checks and adherence to electrical codes, especially in crowded public venues and temporary structures erected for celebrations. Efforts are underway to support the affected families and ensure accountability for the incident.</p><p>What to watch: The ongoing inquiry into safety standards and electrical installations at such public venues.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: Article accurately reflects source summary with appropriate elaboration.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://www.indiatoday.in/india/video/mumbai-ganpati-pandal-electrocution-2-dead-6-injured-at-kala-chowki-site-ytvd-2998663-2026-09-20?utm_source=rss" rel="noopener">India Today</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       <div class="cityguide"><b>City guide</b><p>More on <a href="https://bharatdn.com/city/mumbai/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Mumbai</a> - census 2011 population, live weather and air quality, local food and getaways.</p></div>
